esbible.com/1963/12/31/live-beatles-christmas-show-6/\">Live: The Beatles’ Christmas Show</a></li><li>1962: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1962/12/31/live-star-club-hamburg-75/\">The Beatles live: Star-Club, Hamburg</a></li><li>1960: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1960/12/31/live-casbah-coffee-club-liverpool-2/\">The Beatles live: Casbah Coffee Club, Liverpool</a></li></ul><p>Want more? Visit the <a title=\"Day after day: the Beatles' history\" href=\"/history/\">Beatles history section</a>.</p></div>",
  "textContent": "Heather Louise McCartney was born in Tucson, Arizona, on 31 December 1962. Her birth parents were Linda Eastman and her then-husband Joseph Melville See Jr, who married in June 1962 and divorced in 1965.In 1967 Eastman moved to England with Heather, with See making no objection to her having full custody. Linda met Paul McCartney and the pair married on 12 March 1969. McCartney adopted Heather that same year with See’s approval.The young Heather appeared in The Beatles’ final film, Let It Be, which was filmed in January 1969, although she largely stayed out of the public eye in later years.Heather studied printing at the Photographers’ Workshop in Covent Garden, London, before studying pottery and design and becoming a potter. She later launched a houseware line called Heather McCartney Designs.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPage last updated: 4 November 2025Also on this day...2002: Sir Paul McCartney is presented with his coat of arms1972: John Lennon and Yoko Ono attend New Year party at Mercer Arts Center, New York City1970: Paul McCartney files a lawsuit to dissolve The Beatles’ partnership1966: George Harrison is refused entry to Annabel’s nightclub in London1965: The Beatles attend New Year’s Eve parties1964: Live: Another Beatles Christmas Show1963: Live: The Beatles’ Christmas Show1962: The Beatles live: Star-Club, Hamburg1960: The Beatles live: Casbah Coffee Club, LiverpoolWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
